Overview

This is a prototype machine learning model for detecting Android malware using app permission data.
It demonstrates how ML can distinguish between benign and malicious apps built mainly for testing and learning purposes for our team.

Context

Trained using 10 selected features out of 294 total columns to validate the pipeline.
Model training was done on Curtin University lab computers via SSH, as personal hardware was too slow for the task when train ML model.
This is not the final version future iterations will include the full dataset and optimization.
